From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] authz: resource managers, client contexts and the access check (3711)

authz: resource managers, client contexts and the access check

Every authz function used to fail with ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED. Now:
resource managers (SeAuditPrivilege unless AUTHZ_RM_FLAG_NO_AUDIT, the
dynamic-access and dynamic-group callbacks), client contexts from a token, a
SID (account groups from the local account database) or another context,
AuthzAddSidsToContext, AuthzGetInformationFromContext, and AuthzAccessCheck
with cached results (AuthzCachedAccessCheck, AuthzFreeHandle). The access
check follows the documented DACL rules: ordered ACEs, deny-only and disabled
groups, owner implicit rights and OWNER RIGHTS, PRINCIPAL_SELF, callback ACEs,
privileges for WRITE_OWNER and ACCESS_SYSTEM_SECURITY, restricting SIDs, and
concatenated optional descriptors. AuthzInstall/UninstallSecurityEventSource
write the documented registry values. Object type lists and conditional
expressions are not evaluated (see the notes).
---
